<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SharingRules xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT AND MUST SIT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed
        ABOVE <SharingRules> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        DECISION D17 (2026-08-09). These two rules REPLACE the org-wide NDA__c read that
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit and DPEG_Disposition_View carried as viewAllRecords=true. Both
        sets now hold viewAllRecords=false; their in-root comments carry the full history and
        the supersession note.

        WHY THIS IS NOW POSSIBLE AT ALL. The D12/W3 acceptance said the correct shape was
        "view-all SCOPED TO DISPOSITION NDAs" and that it was "not expressible today: it needs
        record types on NDA__c, which Tranche 3 (decision D7) adds. REVISIT THEN." The record
        types landed in this tranche, so the revisit trigger has fired and the scoping is
        expressible: filter on RecordTypeId.

        OWD VERIFIED, NOT ASSUMED. NDA__c is sharingModel Private with enableSharing true, in
        the repo AND in the target org (retrieved from usman-dpeg 2026-08-09). A sharing rule
        on a Public Read/Write object would be meaningless, so this was checked before the
        grants were narrowed.

        ⚠ TWO RULES, NOT ONE PER PERSONA - AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THE SPLIT.
        A sharing rule shares to a GROUP or ROLE. It cannot target a permission set, so
        "Edit persona" and "View persona" are not addressable here: those are permission-set
        assignments, not group memberships.

        RULE 1 covers BOTH disposition personas with a single Edit-level rule, because
        OBJECT CRUD IS THE CEILING. DPEG_Disposition_View has allowEdit=false, so a View-persona
        holder who is also in DPEG_Acquisitions_Team gets READ ONLY regardless of this rule
        granting Edit. Writing a second Read-level rule to the SAME group would be redundant -
        Salesforce takes the most permissive of overlapping rules - and would double the
        one-at-a-time deploy hazard for no behavioural difference.

        RULE 2 exists for a DIFFERENT POPULATION, not a different access level. The Principals
        hold DPEG_Disposition_View through DPEG_Principal_PSG and are not necessarily members of
        DPEG_Acquisitions_Team. With viewAllRecords gone and only rule 1 in place they would have
        silently lost NDA visibility, and BovController's BOV Outreach pill would report
        "No NDA" for NDAs that exist - the precise defect the D12/W3 acceptance was written to
        prevent. Read is the strictly lower access that persona needs.

        WHY DPEG_Acquisitions_Team. Every other disposition child object in this repo shares to
        that group - Disposition__c, BOV_Submission__c, Wire__c, Disposition_Offer__c,
        Broker_Listing__c all carry a *_Team_RW rule to it at Edit. Using a different group for
        NDA__c would make it the one disposition child with its own population.

        ⚠ CRITERIA-BASED, NOT OWNER-BASED, AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE DEPARTURE from the
        sharingOwnerRules pattern those five objects use. An owner rule shares by who owns the
        row; the requirement here is to share by WHICH KIND of row it is, so that acquisition
        NDAs stay invisible to disposition-only personas no matter who owns them. Only a
        criteria rule can express that.

        ⚠ THE RecordTypeId CRITERIA VALUE IS THE FULLY-QUALIFIED DEVELOPER NAME
        (NDA__c.Disposition_NDA), not an Id - Ids are org-specific and must never be hardcoded
        in metadata. THIS IS THE ONE ELEMENT BELOW WITH NO IN-REPO PRECEDENT: no existing
        sharing rule in this repo filters on RecordTypeId, so the format could not be confirmed
        against a file already known to have passed this org. Confirm it in the check-only
        validation; if it is rejected, the value is the only thing that changes.

        🔴 DEPLOY THESE ONE AT A TIME. A batch deploy of sharing rules rolls ALL of them back in
        this org - established in the 2026-07-22 RBAC build. Two rules means two deploys.

        🔴 GROUP MEMBERSHIP IS NOT DEPLOYABLE METADATA. If DPEG_Acquisitions_Team or Principals
        is empty or wrong in the target org, these rules grant NOTHING and every disposition
        persona sees zero NDAs - which looks exactly like "there are no NDAs". Verify membership
        as a post-deploy gate, and verify it by OPENING A DISPOSITION NDA AS EACH PERSONA, not
        as an administrator.

        🔴 RECALCULATION IS ASYNCHRONOUS. Criteria-based sharing recalculates in the background
        after deploy, and on an object with existing rows it is not instant. A persona checking
        immediately after the deploy may see nothing yet. Do not read that as a failed rule
        until recalculation has completed.

        ACQUISITION NDAs ARE UNAFFECTED. DPEG_Acquisition_Edit / _View and DPEG_Acquisitions keep
        viewAllRecords on NDA__c, so the buy-side module is untouched. These rules only widen
        access to Disposition_NDA rows; they take nothing away from anyone.
    -->
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>NDA_Disposition_Team_RW</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <description>D17: shares disposition NDAs to the disposition working team. Covers BOTH the Edit and View personas - object CRUD is the ceiling, so a DPEG_Disposition_View holder gets read only.</description>
        <label>NDA Disposition Team RW</label>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>RecordTypeId</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>NDA__c.Disposition_NDA</value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Acquisitions_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>NDA_Disposition_Principals_R</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Read</accessLevel>
        <description>D17: shares disposition NDAs to the Principals at Read. A separate rule because principals are a different population, not a different access level - they hold DPEG_Disposition_View via the PSG and may not be in the team group.</description>
        <label>NDA Disposition Principals R</label>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>RecordTypeId</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>NDA__c.Disposition_NDA</value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>Principals</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
</SharingRules>
